{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/120913","id":3988547761,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7tvGix","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120913","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120913.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120913.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120913","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/120913/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/120913/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120913/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/7799b979368a1ff096912280a73dd7b2212354b2","number":120913,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Fix desired size space allocation not respecting minimum sizes correctly","user":{"login":"StarryWorm","id":41305715,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxMzA1NzE1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/41305715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm","html_url":"https://github.com/StarryWorm","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\n- Follow up to #120640 \r\n\r\nIn that PR, I made `BoxContainer` and `GridContainer` (and `FlowContainer`, but that one isn't bugged) allocate space to children whose desired sizes were greater than their minimum sizes. \r\nAs described in the PR, the flow would go: \r\n1. Give each child its minimum size\r\n2. From the remaining space, distribute to children with a desired size\r\n3. If any, from the remaining space, distribute to children with the SIZE_EXPAND flag\r\n\r\nThe problem is, in both cases, the \"remaining space\" computed for step 3, which I used for step 2, also includes the space occupied by the minimum size of the children who have the `SIZE_EXPAND` flag. This is done such that their final sizes are computed irrespective of their minimum sizes, and only take into account the stretch ratios. \r\nHowever, using that in step 2 resulted in the children in step 2 overallocating, using the minimum size of the expanding children as free space to stretch into. This is completely erroneous and results in the step 2 children taking up more space than is available. \r\n\r\nThe images below use `HBoxContainer`, the project has both, but they look the same, so I only put images for one.\r\nBefore:\r\n<img width=\"641\" height=\"52\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6552ea8e-9a48-4a37-82b0-de1fd918d132\" />\r\n\r\nAfter PR:\r\n<img width=\"459\" height=\"54\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/38c706be-2410-40b6-80b8-d8bd9aa29dc4\" />\r\n\r\nProject:\r\n[respect-desired-sizes-mrp.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/29649228/respect-desired-sizes-mrp.zip)\r\n\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\nThe project additionally contains the previous tests from #120640 to ensure no regressions against that PR. \r\n\r\nThis bug slipped through because of a lack of test coverage for the new system, which I should have added earlier. I will work to expand test coverage for these containers so that this kind of oversight does not happen again. ","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":1332303119,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMzMyMzAzMTE5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/regression","name":"regression","description":"","color":"ff63ac","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":1732720779,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxNzMyNzIwNzc5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:gui","name":"topic:gui","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":15520464,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4A7NLQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/25","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/25","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/25/labels","number":25,"state":"open","title":"4.8","description":"","creator":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","si